{"name":"Graham Crust","hex":"#806240","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"graham","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Flour made by grinding wheat berries including the bran.","A graham cracker."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/graham"},{"term":"crust","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A more solid, dense or hard layer on a surface or boundary.","The external, hardened layer of certain foodstuffs, including most types of bread, fried meat, etc."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover with a crust.","To form a crust."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crust"}],"entries":[{"title":"Graham cracker crust","blocks":[{"text":"Graham cracker crust is a style of crumb crust made from crushed graham crackers. Graham crackers are a sweet American cracker made from unbleached, whole wheat graham flour. The crust is usually flavored and stiffened with butter or vegetable oil and sometimes sugar. Graham cracker crust is a very common type of crust for cheesecakes and cream pies in America."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Graham_cracker_crust.jpg/330px-Graham_cracker_crust.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Graham_cracker_crust","wikidata":"Q5593384"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Chocolate_cream_pie.jpg/500px-Chocolate_cream_pie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Chocolate_cream_pie.jpg/1280px-Chocolate_cream_pie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Chocolate_cream_pie.jpg/500px-Chocolate_cream_pie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A chocolate cream pie with a graham cracker crust and macadami